# "due" right before a date makes it a due date; "due" alone, or before a non-date, stays text; case does not matter.
file <<END
INBOX: @inbox
END
keys q
type Pay rent DUE Tomorrow
see Due 
keys <Enter> q
type Pay what is due
keys <Enter> q
type Overdue report today
keys <Enter>
quit
saved <<END
INBOX: @inbox
	- Pay rent @due({today+1})
	- Pay what is due
	- Overdue report @start({today})
END
